44 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129396 #edb/ref 1045 "Graphing Cubic Curves Containing One Distinct Real Root" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129396 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186129988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129396 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129396 #edb/ref 1050 720.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129396 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "bb4f4046-3730-5392-be21-d66c1f2457af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129988 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129988 #edb/ref 1061 21027 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129988 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "051afa25-c36b-5ee0-9d9d-eb0b733f3ede" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129988 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129989 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129989 #edb/ref 1061 21029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129989 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eb11761e-2cec-5933-a69a-8624ea5f99b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129989 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129990 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129991 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129990 #edb/ref 1061 21032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129990 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "865f0324-f2f1-593d-a63c-922f8ee140ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129990 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129991 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129991 #edb/ref 1061 21033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129991 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d1f3375e-451a-5569-acec-c0bde4d976fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129991 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129994 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129994 #edb/ref 1061 21037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129994 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "25f7fb47-95e9-58de-9b40-bdc5ea29bc79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129994 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129999 #edb/ref 1061 21043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129999 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c6e25844-0c2f-5a68-af2d-f3b6ac122e86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129999 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130361 #edb/ref 1064 "The graph of any cubic function $y = f(x)= ax^3 + bx^2 + cx +d,$ where $a >0,$ has a characteristic inverted ${\\textsf{S}}$-shape, with $y$-values ranging from $-\\infty$ to $+\\infty.$ This means that every such function has at least one real root and at most three distinct roots. \n\nFor instance, suppose that we want to plot the graph of $y = x^3-3x^2 +3x-1.$ First, we need to find the roots, so we set $y=0$ and solve. Noting that the polynomial is a perfect cube, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+3x-1 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get one real root $x=1,$ which has multiplicity $3.$ \n\nAt a root of multiplicity $3,$ the graph becomes **tangent** (i.e., lies parallel) to the $x$-axis and crosses the $x$-axis. \n\nTherefore, the graph looks as follows:\n\n![](images/d8/d87834ef3f7225b00d92e6051a67735cf6695c5a2eff9635c4de416d0be1577f.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130361 #edb/ref 1065 3752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130361 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "848b066b-7e36-58cf-ae75-a8e28e9d3358" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130361 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130364 #edb/ref 1064 "The graph of any cubic function $y = f(x)= ax^3 + bx^2 + cx +d,$ where $a <0,$ has a characteristic ${\\textsf{S}}$-shape, with $y$-values ranging from $+\\infty$ to $-\\infty.$\n\nFor instance, suppose that we want to plot the graph of $y = -x^3+3x^2 -3x+1.$ First, we need to find the roots, so we set $y=0$ and solve. Noting that the polynomial is a perfect cube, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-3x+1 & =0 \\\\ (-x+1)^{3} & =0 \\\\ -(x-1)^{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get one real root $x=1,$ which has multiplicity $3.$ \n\nAt a root of multiplicity $3,$ the graph becomes tangent to the $x$-axis and crosses the $x$-axis. Therefore, the graph looks as follows:\n\n![](images/5c/5cd99c1f2a3a596002edc222e0d9b13969286a49361fc804fe7db8818017980b.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130364 #edb/ref 1065 3756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130364 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "73e1e583-b344-5de0-9cc8-c0ec3a475e82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130364 #edb/ref 1067 "Negative Cubic Curves With Only One Distinct Real Root" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
